 "briefing": "# Zepto Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Status of This Briefing\n\nResearch for this window could not be completed. Every search attempt returned a rate-limit error, so no news, product launches, hires, or deals from 16 October to 15 November 2026 have been verified. The briefing therefore contains no unverified claims, and no facts have been added from memory.\n\n## What Could Not Be Verified\n\n- **General news and corporate developments:** No items confirmed for the window.\n- **Product, service, or feature launches:** No items confirmed. This includes dark store formats, new categories, new cities, and app features.\n- **Executive and other hires or departures:** No items confirmed at C-suite, board, or senior leadership level.\n- **Deals:** No funding rounds, investments, acquisitions or acquisition talks, partnerships, commercial agreements, or IPO-related filings confirmed for the window.\n- **Items just outside the window:** None gathered, so no earlier or later context can be given with confidence.\n\nBecause no sources were retrieved, the dates and details for each category cannot be confirmed. Any announcement from the window should be treated as unknown until it is checked directly against the sources below.\n\n## Recommended Checks Before 17 November\n\nThe following primary sources should be checked first, in this order:\n\n1. Zepto's official website, including its newsroom, press releases, and blog, at [Zepto official website](https://www.zepto.com).\n2. Zepto's official social media accounts and the public accounts of its founders and executives.\n3. Stock exchange and Registrar of Companies filings, which would show any funding, share allotment, or corporate restructuring.\n\nReputable outlets to check next, filtered to 16 October to 15 November 2026, are Economic Times, Mint, Moneycontrol, Business Standard, Reuters, Bloomberg, Inc42, Entrackr, and TechCrunch. The research tool did not return results from any of these, so each item should be confirmed by opening the original page.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which announcements, launches, leadership changes, or deals has Zepto made since 16 October 2026, and where has it published them? This is needed because no verified public record of the window could be assembled.\n2. Has Zepto raised, committed, or agreed any new funding, investment, acquisition, or commercial partnership in the past month, and what is the current status of any IPO preparation?\n3. What has changed in Zepto's product or operating footprint in the past month, such as new categories, dark store formats, cities, or app features, and what is planned for the next quarter?\n\n### Sources\n\n[1] Zepto official website (primary source to check; content not verified in this research): https://www.zepto.com",
